// viewray — the one direction the sky is asked about.
//
// Its own module for a reason that is not ceremony: the sky's colour lives in
// `atmosphere` and the cloud deck in `clouddome`, `atmosphere` already reads the
// deck, and both are asked the same question — what is along this direction.
// Declaring the question in either one would point the dependency back at the
// other. Declared here, both simply read it.
//
// The length arrives inverted because every caller has it that way already: the
// gradient's per-row setup divides once and hands the reciprocal down the
// scanline, and a caller with a unit direction passes one.

/** A world-space view direction through a pixel, with its length already inverted. */
struct ViewRay {
    pub(crate) dx : f64,
    pub(crate) dy : f64,
    pub(crate) dz : f64,
    pub(crate) inv : f64,
}
